{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #529: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $d_k(n)$ be the expected distance from the origin after taking $n$ random steps from the origin in $\\mathbb{Z}^k$ (conditional on no self intersections) - that is, a self-avoiding walk. Is it true that\\[\\lim_{n\\to \\infty}\\frac{d_2(n)}{n^{1/2}}= \\infty?\\]Is it true that\\[d_k(n)\\ll n^{1/2}\\]for $k\\geq 3$? Current best: Hara and Slade (\\cite{HaSl91} and \\cite{HaSl92}) proved this for all $k\\geq 5$. Prize: no. Tags: geometry, probability."},"claim_id":"vcl_0d2d5ca1c984d5862813f5006300bffdcbf730e5428ccde29c131f5b1d86b76f","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:529","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_cd1b57093dcb221f","object_root":"sha256:2a5096ede2aee74b2703fe6014e62dbb02f0a732a5c907a2b321454e5005cb19","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:529"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}